# Example crontab for a daily cycle. cron fires on wall-clock weekdays; the trading-day guard
# (python -m swingcore.trading_day_guard) is what skips NYSE holidays. It exits 1 on a closed day and
# 255 when it cannot tell (e.g. the holiday calendar does not cover the year); either way the cycle
# after `&&` never starts, and on 255 the error line reaches cron's mail.
#
# CRON_TZ is a cronie extension (Fedora/RHEL/Arch). Debian/Ubuntu's stock cron ignores it and fires
# on the machine's timezone, so there either set the machine to America/New_York or use the systemd
# timer in deploy/systemd, whose OnCalendar= carries its own timezone.
CRON_TZ=America/New_York
SHELL=/bin/bash

# m  h  dom mon dow  command
30   7  *   *   1-5  cd "$HOME/swing-trading-showcase" && mkdir -p cache && .venv/bin/python -m swingcore.trading_day_guard --quiet && .venv/bin/python -m swingcore.demo --dry-run --out "cache/$(date +\%F)-morning.json"
